Subject: Check native graphics pools and frame lifecycle

Upstream-base: 2c5c51e483b652d178ef06a44b83b07a0f97d2a6

Check native graphics pools and frame lifecycle
Preserve pointer-width addresses and resource marks, align both halves of the
double buffers independently while retaining their original logical budgets,
validate arithmetic and reject allocation before publishing invalid offsets.
Allocate MEM1/MEM2 transactionally and always restore CurrentAllocator. Run
inventory releases before freeing backing pools; reclaim game-owned pool
objects explicitly. Add repeatable ordered shutdown and reject foreign markers,
invalid nesting, unexpected pool handles and repeated initialization.
Native frame advancement requires an explicit cache-invalidation provider.
The scene supplies real GX invalidations; a missing provider stops explicitly.
Keep console paths and original memory labels unchanged. This is a memory/static
inventory subset, not glStartup or a complete native graphics implementation.

